        "spell_check": false,
        "word_limit_enabled": false
      },
      "item_body": "<p>A 200 kg crate is pulled 10 m up a 20\u00b0 incline by a force of 1200 N applied parallel to the incline. The coefficient of kinetic friction between the crate and the ramp is \u03bc = 0.25. (a) Describe the free-body diagram of the crate (list each force and its direction), and compute, showing all steps, the work done by the applied force, the work done by gravity, and the work done by friction. (b) Find the net work done on the crate. (c) Explain, in full sentences, what the sign of the net work tells you about how the crate's speed changes as it moves up the ramp, referring to the work-energy principle.</p>",
      "user_response_type": "Text",
